<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10892" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contrectātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contract-</span></b> ), ōnis. f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				touching, touch, contact</i> (very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equae, vaccae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 27, 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam contrectationes et amores soluti et
					liberi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rep. 4, 4, 4</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Dig. 41, 2, 3, §
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In the jurists, <i>an illegal appropriation of a thing
				to one's self, stealing, theft</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 47, 2, 1, § 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 2, 31, 29</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
